1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,935
The missing voice belonged to a clown at the children's ceremony during the settlement week.

2
00:00:04,935 --> 00:00:10,715
“You never asked the age of the people who will live under this roof,” he said.

3
00:00:10,715 --> 00:00:18,425
“You have a purpose and a vote, and you have not asked whether the house is impossible to heat.”

4
00:00:18,425 --> 00:00:27,490
The apparent answer was attractive: select a smaller unit, choose a cautious price, and forget the rest.

5
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:43,536
“Sorrow is not a clinical condition,” he said, “and a guidance note is not counsel.” A stir in the hall made the identification of the real problem evident: there was no equality in the plan.

6
00:00:43,536 --> 00:00:47,351
The equality he meant was measured in decades.

7
00:00:47,351 --> 00:00:52,256
“A materialist reads a house as an asset,” he said.

8
00:00:52,256 --> 00:01:07,331
“A materialist should also read it as a lifetime.” His idealism, he admitted, was cheerful and his realism was not; the seeming contradiction was the whole of his argument.

9
00:01:07,331 --> 00:01:13,656
The solidity of the building was never in doubt, and the eternity of a mortgage was.

10
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:21,221
“You can visualize a family in it, and you cannot visualize a family paying for it,” he said.

11
00:01:21,221 --> 00:01:26,091
“A clear-cut plan would say who repays and when.”

12
00:01:26,091 --> 00:01:31,561
The blame for the confusion lay with the guidance, not with the family.

13
00:01:31,561 --> 00:01:37,916
“A cautious buyer and a cheating seller can look alike on paper,” Maya wrote.

14
00:01:37,916 --> 00:01:47,046
“The difference is the second page.” The voice he raised was mad by their standards and just by his own.

15
00:01:47,046 --> 00:01:54,696
The settlement was revised by one clause: every unit would be sold with a heating assessment attached.

16
00:01:54,696 --> 00:02:03,231
It was almost nothing, and it was nearly everything, and the group agreed to appear at the next meeting with the figure.

17
00:02:03,231 --> 00:02:08,121
They agreed almost at once, and I nearly said nothing.

18
00:02:08,121 --> 00:02:15,021
We need a similar kind of free claim, and a true history is not a chapter that dies.

19
00:02:15,021 --> 00:02:22,141
A kind moment, an image, and a win were not enough while nearly half the residents were absent.

20
00:02:22,141 --> 00:02:31,696
The break in the plan appeared as a missing page, and almost everyone who could vote did; the need was similar to the earlier survey.

21
00:02:31,696 --> 00:02:43,751
We must decide whether the dead govern us; a house is alive in a way that materialism cannot visualise, and the death of the old plan did not settle the question.

22
00:02:43,751 --> 00:02:49,022
The settlement would visualise the cost instead.
